CODEGEN.md §3.3, §3.5 (the C++ name plan, decision 37): fields `A` and `a` both give the C++ getter GetA, one class scope, so check refuses what gen/cpp would.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A thing.
record Thing {
  /// Its key.
  a: Int
  /// Another.
  A: Int @json("c")
}

/// The things.
let things: [Thing] keyed by a = [{ a: 1, A: 2 }]

emit cpp { out: "@features/a", namespace: "a", mode: data }
emit json { out: "out/" }
